00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.270
So let's talk about the nine most
commonly made mistakes

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:08.429
nearly everyone makes doing keto, okay?
Number one: doing it without intermittent

00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:14.519
fasting. Now the whole purpose of keto is to fix insulin, to actually lower insulin,

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:18.240
to fix insulin resistance. And why
not add intermittent fasting? Because

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.160
every time you eat, you raise insulin. So
if you just do ketosis without

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.880
intermittent fasting, you may not lose
weight especially, if you're eating like

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.500
six meals a day. So it's number one.
Number two: eating when you're not hungry.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.000
So it's like, if you're not hungry and
you eat, what's going to happen is you're

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.559
going to spike insulin again. So here you
were, you're sleeping all night, you're

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:44.640
burning fat, you're not hungry in the
morning, yet you eat. Well, your body was

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.510
in fat-burning all night long. So now
it's going to not be in fat-burning because

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:54.510
you just ate. So I would not eat unless
you're hungry, alright? Number three:

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.620
eating too much protein. So when you
consume too much protein, you can

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.149
stimulate insulin as well. So in your
mind sometimes, if you're working out, you

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:07.229
think, "Oh, I need more protein." But in
reality, all you need is between three to

00:01:07.229 --> 00:01:12.030
six ounces per meal. It's much better to
consume more vegetables, a little more

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.229
fat than excessive amounts of protein,
okay? The only exception is if you're

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:20.310
let's say, 18-years-old and your
metabolism is super-high. You can get

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:26.640
away with a little bit more. Okay, number
four: omitting the vegetables. So in this

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.210
situation, if you don't consume enough
vegetables, you're not going to get the

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:34.950
potassium you need to form the protein
on your body parts. You're not going to

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:39.570
get the potassium to help regulate the
heart, the muscles, because it's a main

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:44.189
electrolyte. You need a tremendous amount
of potassium and that comes from

00:01:44.189 --> 00:01:48.509
vegetables. Seven to ten cups of
vegetables every single day. You're going to

00:01:48.509 --> 00:01:51.570
have to bite the bullet and do that. And
also, without vegetables, you can't flush

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:56.759
all the fat coming out through the liver.
Number five: focusing too much on the

00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:01.380
weight or the keto sticks. So a lot of
times when you weigh yourself, you're

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.729
like, "Wow, I'm not losing much weight." But your stomach is shrinking. Realize that

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:10.289
you're ,when you're doing this, you are
actually converting more of your energy

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:14.150
to making muscle
and you're losing fat but you're

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.840
actually building up more muscle. And
muscle weighs a little bit more, so it

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.970
might not show up on the scale. So don't
sweat it. Go by your waist to see if your

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.970
waist is shrinking. And so, the same thing
with the keto sticks. If you're not in

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:30.440
ketosis, it doesn't mean anything because
you could be utilizing ketones. Ketones

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.540
are the byproduct of fat burning, okay? So
if you're very efficient and you're

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:39.440
burning up all this fat, it's not going
to show up in the urine. Number seven: too

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.830
much or too little fat. So this is the
variable that you need to really pay

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:46.519
attention to because if you have too
much, it could overload the gallbladder

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:50.510
and the liver and cause right shoulder
pain. If you don't have enough, you might

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.900
not be able to make it from one meal to
the next, so you're gonna be hungry but

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.799
as you do this, and your system is more
efficient, and you're burning more of

00:02:57.799 --> 00:03:02.209
your fat, you'll need less dietary fat.
Okay, number eight: allowing too many

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:06.260
carbohydrates, okay? Now if you really
have a person to a food log and they

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.819
start looking at the hidden carbs, you're
going to find that it's like exceeding that

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:15.829
50-gram limit per day. I like to keep my
carbs below 30 grams every single day.

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:19.040
However, you don't have to worry about
calculating the vegetables because we

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.359
want you to consume a lot of vegetables,
okay? Number nine: worrying about the

00:03:23.359 --> 00:03:26.450
cholesterol. And this is a big one
because think about it, here you are

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:30.349
releasing fat from the fat cells. What
does that mean? That means you're

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:36.349
releasing triglycerides and cholesterol.
So when you do that, what do you think is

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:41.959
going to happen in your blood? It's going to go up, so I put a link down below so you

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:45.769
can get the full understanding of what
that means. But it's not going to be a

00:03:45.769 --> 00:03:48.500
problem, alright? Thanks for watching.

